## 📊 TASK 3: Instrument Monitoring & Alerting

### ✅ Objective:
Ensure observability of end-to-end latency and trigger alerts when P99 exceeds 75ms.

### ✅ Implementation:

#### 1. **OpenTelemetry + AWS X-Ray Integration**

Add tracing context to profile retrieval flow:

```js
const { trace } = require('@opentelemetry/api');

async function getUserProfileWithTrace(userId) {
  const span = trace.getActiveSpan();
  const subSpan = span.startSpan('fetch_user_profile_from_s3');

  try {
    const result = await getUserProfile(userId);
    subSpan.end();
    return result;
  } catch (err) {
    subSpan.recordException(err);
    subSpan.end();
    throw err;
  }
}
```

> ✅ X-Ray will capture:
> - Duration of S3 call
> - Redis cache hit/miss
> - Total request duration

#### 2. **CloudWatch Alarms (P99 > 75ms)**

Create alarm via Terraform:

```hcl
resource "aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm" "p99_latency_alert" {
  alarm_name          = "api-p99-latency-exceeds-75ms"
  comparison_operator = "GreaterThanThreshold"
  evaluation_periods  = 1
  metric_name         = "Latency"
  namespace           = "AWS/ApiGateway"
  period              = 60
  statistic           = "P99"
  threshold           = 75.0
  treat_missing_data  = "missing"

  dimensions = {
    ApiName = "UserProfileAPI"
    Stage   = "prod"
  }

  alarm_actions = [aws_sns_topic.alerts.arn]
}
```

> ✅ Alarm triggers SNS → DevOps team notified within seconds.

